From: Dr. Utsugi <cidwel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ath: force a world-roaming regdomain (this card is CN-locked)

The wcn3990 in the POCO X3 NFC ships its regulatory EEPROM programmed to
China (regdomain 0x809c -> country CN). China's 5 GHz plan omits the mid
band, 5470-5730 MHz (channels 100-144), so any access point that Wi-Fi's
automatic DFS channel selection puts there is completely invisible to the
phone -- it cannot even see the network, let alone join it. In Europe that
is where a large share of 5 GHz routers land.

There is no runtime lever for this. ath registers the wiphy with
REGULATORY_STRICT_REG | REGULATORY_CUSTOM_REG and derives the domain from
the EEPROM at init, so a userspace `iw reg set <cc>` never reaches the card
(measured: the global domain changes, phy#0 stays CN). The country is fixed
when the driver probes.

So fix it there: force an Atheros world-roaming SKU (0x67), whose table is
2.4 GHz channels 1-13 plus ATH_5GHZ_ALL = 5150-5350 and 5470-5850 MHz -- the
mid band included. Those channels come up passive (NL80211_RRF_NO_IR), which
is the legal world-roaming behaviour and is enough for a station: a passive
scan hears the beacon, and ath's own beacon_found path then clears NO_IR so
the phone can associate and transmit. 0x67 is chosen over the sanitizer's
default 0x64, whose table uses ATH_5GHZ_NO_MIDBAND and would skip exactly the
channels we need.

Applied only on the initial probe (ath_regd_init), so the dynamic country
path (__ath_regd_init from ath_reg_dyn_country) is left untouched.

Signed-off-by: Dr. Utsugi <cidwel@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/regd.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/regd.c	2026-09-15 13:09:04.122350018 +0200
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/regd.c	2026-09-15 13:09:04.146006379 +0200
@@ -764,6 +764,16 @@
 						 regulatory);
 	int r;
 
+	/*
+	 * This card is EEPROM-locked to CN (regdomain 0x809c), whose 5 GHz
+	 * plan omits channels 100-144, making networks there invisible. The
+	 * wiphy is STRICT_REG|CUSTOM_REG so `iw reg set` never reaches it;
+	 * the only lever is here. Force an Atheros world-roaming SKU (0x67)
+	 * whose table includes 5470-5850 MHz. The mid band comes up passive
+	 * (NO_IR): legal, and enough for a station once the beacon is heard.
+	 */
+	reg->current_rd = 0x67;
+
 	r = __ath_regd_init(reg);
 	if (r)
 		return r;
